.TH SDL_HINT_WINDOWS_RAW_MOUSE_NOLEGACY 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_WINDOWS_RAW_MOUSE_NOLEGACY \- A variable controlling whether the RIDEV_NOLEGACY flag is set when enabling Windows raw mouse events.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_WINDOWS_RAW_MOUSE_NOLEGACY \(dqSDL_WINDOWS_RAW_MOUSE_NOLEGACY\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If RIDEV_NOLEGACY is set, then Windows mouse events will not be sent for mouse motion while relative mode is enabled\[char46] This improves performance when players are using high DPI mice, but should be disabled while showing custom assert dialogs in your application code\[char46]
.PP
Caution: Windows will not see mouse button releases in relative mode with this active\[char46] This means you should not enable relative mode while a mouse button is currently pressed\[char46]
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Windows mouse events will be generated while relative motion is enabled\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Windows mouse events will not be generated while relative motion is enabled\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]6\[char46]0\[char46]

